interp-only: this fixture drives the peer with an interpreter `async` fiber, so
it only runs under the cooperative session-channel runtime of `tur --interpret`
(tests/run-turi.sh).  The compiled suite (tests/run.sh) skips it: under the
compiled pthread session runtime a session recv inside a cooperative async
fiber has no separate thread to rendezvous with.  See
docs/archive/turi-session-types-plan.md (Slice B).
